Global open burning and non-burned waste shares
------------------------------------------------

The package calculates global open burning and non-burned waste shares from
Cottom, Cook, and Velis (2024), *A local-to-global emissions inventory of
macroplastic pollution*, Nature 633, 101-108, DOI
10.1038/s41586-024-07758-6, and its Dryad dataset, DOI
10.5061/dryad.8cz8w9gxb. Dryad publishes datasets under the CC0 instrument.
pyToCE distributes the calculated fate shares, route selections and
material mappings. It does not redistribute the article or the 1.45 GB Dryad
dataset. The open-dump infiltration weights have a separate licensed source:
preparation derives them once from the ecoinvent 3.12 RoW polyethylene waste
market and saves them only in the prepared workspace. They are not Cottom data
and are not covered by the Dryad CC0 instrument.

The package models the non-burned remainder with an open dump LCI; it is not a
measured H12 dumping share. The treatment activities and their exchanges remain
in each licensed Brightway workspace.

ecoinvent
---------

ecoinvent 3.12 Allocation, cut-off by classification, and the ecoinvent 3.12
LCIA implementation workbook are user-supplied licensed inputs. They are
not distributed by pyToCE. Generated activity codes, exchanges,
crosswalks, matrices, characterization factors, and other licensed derivatives
remain in the prepared workspace.

Methane density source
----------------------

The direct air capture methane inventory uses the NIST Chemistry
WebBook, Standard Reference Database 69 (DOI 10.18434/T4D303), implementation
of the Setzmann–Wagner methane equation of state (DOI 10.1063/1.555898). The package
uses the reported pure-methane density of 0.67983 kg/m3 at 288.15 K and
0.101325 MPa only to convert the DAC methane service between mass and the
ecoinvent standard-volume unit. It is not used for another methane route,
emission, yield, or inventory adjustment.

USLCI/ACC ABS unit-process data
-------------------------------

The retained USLCI ABS attribution identifies the non-confidential North
American unit process in USLCI 1.2026-06.0. The source process is UUID
0e42a306-ee2d-362e-8bc3-580000096459, version 00.01.009, at data-repository
commit a900b507109a80c21db983e5f13f283f4a84aa51:

https://www.lcacommons.gov/lca-collaboration/National_Renewable_Energy_Laboratory/USLCI_Database_Public/dataset/PROCESS/0e42a306-ee2d-362e-8bc3-580000096459?commitId=a900b507109a80c21db983e5f13f283f4a84aa51

The publication-source UUID is fb5e258c-aee8-4c18-af99-fd993391a0b0:

